Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; RTX 5080 GPU timeout fix -- double-click this file, then approve the prompts.
; A reboot is required before it takes effect.
;
; WHAT IT FIXES
; Windows kills and resets the graphics driver if a single GPU operation takes
; longer than 2 seconds (TdrDelay) or 5 seconds (TdrDdiDelay). Those defaults are
; tuned for games and desktop drawing, not for AI video generation, where one
; denoising step on a 19-billion-parameter model can legitimately run longer.
;
; On 2026-08-05 at 23:58:08 exactly that happened: the driver reset mid-render,
; which invalidated the CUDA context underneath the running job. WanGP never
; noticed the context was gone and hung waiting on it, so a 60-second video that
; was 6 of 7 clips complete sat frozen for 29 minutes and then died with nothing
; written. The Windows log shows the same driver-reset event firing every 5-6
; minutes throughout render sessions -- each one recoverable, until it wasn't.
;
; This raises both limits to 60 seconds. This box currently has NO override set
; at all, so it is running the 2-second default.
;
; THE TRADEOFF
; If the GPU ever hangs for real, Windows now waits up to 60 seconds before
; resetting it instead of 2. During that window the screen can be black or
; frozen. That is the accepted tradeoff on a machine used for GPU compute; it is
; the standard recommendation for this workload.
;
; TO UNDO: double-click UNDO_gpu_timeout.reg in this same folder, then reboot.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers]
"TdrDelay"=dword:0000003c
"TdrDdiDelay"=dword:0000003c
